    "title": "National Burrito Day 2026: Deals and freebies from Chipotle, QDOBA and more",
    "text": "Chains are offering BOGO meals, free burritos and discounted menu items, with many deals tied to rewards programs and apps. National Burrito Day is Thursday, April 2, and several restaurant chains across the country are offering deals and freebies to help fans celebrate. The burrito — a staple Mexican dish typically filled with ingredients like beans, rice, meat, cheese and vegetables wrapped in a tortilla — has become a go-to favorite for everything from quick meals to over-the-top creations. Find out what restaurants are offering for National Burrito Day below. Chipotle Chipotle is offering $0 delivery fees on orders placed through its app and website on April 2. The chain also brought back its Burrito Vault game leading up to the holiday, giving players a chance to win free burritos for a year, BOGO deals and other rewards. QDOBA QDOBA Rewards members can get a free entrée when they purchase an entrée and a drink. The deal is available April 2 and can be redeemed in-store, online or through the app. Del Taco Del Taco is offering a free classic burrito to Del Yeah! Rewards members who make a $3 purchase. The deal is valid only on April 2 and can be redeemed online or through the app. Moe’s Southwest Grill Moe’s Southwest Grill is offering a buy one, get one free deal on burritos, bowls and More Value Meals for the holiday. 7-Eleven At participating 7-Eleven, Speedway and Stripes locations, customers can grab a chicken fajita burrito for $5. Baja Fresh Baja Fresh is offering $5 chicken Baja Burritos on April 2. Rewards members who make a purchase will also receive a coupon for $5 off a future order of $20 or more. California Tortilla Customers who buy any burrito on April 2 will receive a $10 reward to use on a future purchase.",
